---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Pagination from "../../components/Pagination.astro";
import Picture from "../../components/Picture.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Balto" pathname="/work/balto/" caseStudy={true}>
  <div class="case-study">
    <div class="case-study-header">
      <div class="case-study-header-content constrain">
        <h1>Balto</h1>
        <div class="case-study-header-nav">
          <a title="Previous" href="/work/gtreasury/"
            ><Pagination name="previous" /></a
          >
          <a title="Next" href="/work/kuali/"><Pagination name="next" /></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="case-study-overview">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Role:</strong> Product designer
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The challenge:</strong> Transitioning a proprietary real-time AI
          engine from an isolated desktop widget into a scalable enterprise coaching
          and QA platform.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Top outcome:</strong> Designed and delivered a comprehensive set
          of high-fidelity prototypes for Real-Time Coaching, establishing the foundational
          product architecture and aligning leadership around a shared vision.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="case-study-content pswp-gallery">
      <h2>From desktop widget to enterprise platform</h2>
      <p>
        Balto builds AI-driven listening software that analyzes live call center
        audio to stream real-time guidance. While the core engine was highly
        effective, its original value was confined to a narrow desktop widget
        focused strictly on agent-facing metrics—making it difficult to sell
        into large enterprise operations.
      </p>
      <p>
        To expand into real-time coaching and quality assurance (QA) markets,
        leadership initiated an aggressive product overhaul. I joined as a
        contract product designer to partner with product leadership,
        translating raw machine learning capabilities into a cohesive,
        multi-user platform strategy.
      </p>
      <div class="case-study-image-block">
        <figure class="case-study-image-solo">
          <Picture
            name="balto-sketch"
            alt="Low-fidelity wireframes mapping out real-time call center coaching workflows"
            caption="Translating raw AI engine capabilities into low-fidelity structural flows and wireframes."
            showCaption={false}
            lightbox
          />
          <figcaption class="case-study-image-caption">
            Translating raw AI engine capabilities into low-fidelity structural
            flows and wireframes.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <h2>Architecting the coaching ecosystem</h2>
      <p>
        Expanding into call center operations required designing for distinct
        user roles simultaneously: agents handling live calls, supervisors
        monitoring teams in real time, and administrators managing QA rules.
      </p>
      <p>
        Working alongside the product manager, I mapped complex feature
        requirements into discrete interaction patterns. We established core
        workflows for real-time agent prompts, automated event triggers, and
        supervisor intervention tools built to handle live, high-stress
        environments.
      </p>
      <div class="case-study-image-block">
        <figure>
          <div class="case-study-image-grid">
            <Picture
              name="balto-add-alert"
              alt="Add new alert modal interface for setting up rule-based real-time AI triggers"
              caption="Alert builder: Setting up rule-based trigger criteria, target agents, and associated playbooks for real-time monitoring."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
            <Picture
              name="balto-alert-browser"
              alt="Call monitoring card showing flagged compliance alerts, action controls, and a live call transcript snippet"
              caption="Live call monitor: Displaying real-time AI alert triggers, conversation transcripts, and supervisor intervention controls."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
            <Picture
              name="balto-call-score"
              alt="Agent call evaluation dashboard showing automated category scores and checklist compliance popover"
              caption="Call evaluation view: Aggregating AI checklist compliance, section scores, and overall call performance metrics."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
            <Picture
              name="balto-criteria-builder"
              alt="Playbook rule configuration interface mapping phrase criteria, presence requirements, and point weights"
              caption="Playbook builder: Defining phrase match rules, presence requirements, and scoring weights for real-time prompt triggers."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="case-study-image-caption">
            Core interface patterns defining agent assistance, real-time
            supervisor alerts, and administrative rule creation.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <h2>High-stakes, real-time feedback</h2>
      <p>
        Call center operations move fast, and cognitive overload is a constant
        risk. When the AI detects a critical moment on a call, the supervisor
        needs immediate context to decide whether to listen in, send a direct
        coaching tip, or take over the call entirely.
      </p>
      <p>
        I created high-fidelity prototype flows to stress-test these high-stakes
        interactions. We refined density, visual hierarchy, and status
        indicators so supervisors could evaluate agent performance and trigger
        interventions in seconds without disrupting ongoing operations.
      </p>
      <div class="case-study-image-block">
        <figure>
          <div class="case-study-image-grid">
            <Picture
              name="balto-alerts"
              alt="Balto web application interface showing configured alerts table alongside a live supervisor feed and chat sidebar"
              caption="Real-Time Coaching alerts: Managing system-wide alert rules alongside live supervisor monitoring and agent chat panels."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
            <Picture
              name="balto-config"
              alt="QA Scorecard builder interface displaying call evaluation categories, percentage weights, and scorecard configuration settings"
              caption="Scorecard builder: Configuring evaluation categories, weighted scoring models, and compliance criteria for call auditing."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
            <Picture
              name="balto-log"
              alt="Activity Log interface showing agent alert counts, call logs, and expandable supervisor chat histories"
              caption="Activity log: Tracking historical alert volumes across agent teams with inspectable chat transcripts and call records."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
            <Picture
              name="balto-loading"
              alt="Balto reporting dashboard interface displaying a central loading spinner with the message We're crunching the numbers..."
              caption="Loading state: Displaying feedback during asynchronous data fetching and report generation."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="case-study-image-caption">
            High-fidelity prototype flows evaluating live supervisor
            interventions and post-call performance scoring views.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <h2>Aligning stakeholders and scaling the vision</h2>
      <p>
        To keep engineering and executive leadership aligned, I facilitated
        rapid, daily review cycles using detailed Figma prototypes. Working
        closely with the lead designer, I helped integrate evolving visual
        patterns and brand standards into a unified component library.
      </p>
      <p>
        The resulting product architecture transformed Balto from a
        point-solution widget into a complete real-time coaching platform,
        providing the foundational product strategy needed to drive their
        enterprise expansion.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
